Why vendored: the agent build is JDK-only (no Maven or Gradle) and must
work offline, at build and test time. `mage agentBuild` checks the
SHA-256 above before using the jar, then relocates its classes to
iormesh.agent.shaded.asm (agent/tools/Relocate.java) so the agent never
clashes with an ASM the traced application ships. LICENSE.txt ships in
the agent jar as META-INF/LICENSE-asm.txt, as BSD-3 asks of binary
redistributions.

Why this version: 9.11.1 reads class files up to Java 28 (Opcodes.V28)
and is itself Java 5 bytecode, so it runs on the agent's JDK 17 floor
(PLAN.md decision #29) and parses the JDK classes of 17 through 27-ea.

To update: download the new asm-<v>.jar from Maven Central, compare its
SHA-1 with the published .sha1, replace the jar and LICENSE.txt, and
update the version, both hashes here and asmJar/asmSHA256 in
magefile_agent.go in the same commit.
